VisualOn AAC encoder library

This library contains an encoder implementation of the Advanced Audio
Coding (AAC) audio codec. The library is based on a codec implementation
by VisualOn as part of the Stagefright framework from the Google
Android project.

Live bit-rate reconfiguration
------------------------------

VO_PID_AAC_LIVE_BITRATE changes the encoder target bit rate on a
continuous stream without reopening the encoding core. The sample rate
and channel count stay unchanged and the accumulated psychoacoustic,
block-switching, bit-reservoir and threshold-adaptation history is kept.

The parameter is a pointer to VO_S32 holding a bit rate in bit/s:

    VO_S32 bitrate = 96000;
    hCodec->SetParam(hCodec, VO_PID_AAC_LIVE_BITRATE, &bitrate);

A SetParam call only stores the request; it is applied to the next fully
encoded 1024-sample frame. Feeding partial input never applies it and
never discards the half frame held inside the encoder. GetParam returns
the bit rate currently in effect:

    VO_S32 current;
    hCodec->GetParam(hCodec, VO_PID_AAC_LIVE_BITRATE, &current);

Legal values are 4000..160000 bit/s per channel and at most
sampleRate*6*nChannels in total. Out-of-range values, null handles and
null pointers return VO_ERR_INVALID_ARG; the value is never silently
corrected. The latest legal request wins; an illegal request does not
overwrite a queued one. Setting the bit rate already in effect cancels a
queued change (or is a no-op when nothing is queued).

The legacy VO_PID_AAC_ENCPARAM entry point still works exactly as before
and reinitializes the core, resetting its history.

Building and testing without autotools
--------------------------------------

The development checks compile everything with the system C compiler and
libc only:

    sh devcheck/baseline.sh   # original library + legacy reset demo, 96 frames
    sh devcheck/target.sh     # modified library + tests/live_bitrate.c + example

The five test groups print AAC_LIVE_CASE <name> PASS for phase, history,
reservoir, streaming and compatibility.

Manual builds:

    cc -std=c99 -D__unused= -Iaacenc/inc -Iaacenc/basic_op -Icommon/include \
       common/cmnMemory.c aacenc/basic_op/*.c aacenc/src/*.c -c
    ar rcs libvo-aacenc.a *.o

    cc -std=c99 -D__unused= -Iaacenc/inc -Iaacenc/basic_op -Icommon/include \
       tests/live_bitrate.c libvo-aacenc.a -o live_bitrate
    cc -std=c99 -D__unused= -Iaacenc/inc -Iaacenc/basic_op -Icommon/include \
       examples/live_bitrate_example.c libvo-aacenc.a -o live_bitrate_example

The example writes a continuous ADTS file and switches the bit rate at
frames 32 and 64:

    ./live_bitrate_example output.aac

